  "slug": "colored-indexes-832d",
  "summary": "Recent preprints report batch-updatable colored indexes, faster and smaller k-mer dictionaries, and compressed-space matching across pangenome assemblies.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is compressed, sequence-aware indexing for large collections of genomes and k-mers. Two SBWT-based works address colored and k-mer dictionaries. One extracts, removes, and set-combines colored k-mer indexes in batches without original sequences, with results matching from-scratch builds. The other pairs batched, prefetching queries with single-orientation storage, reporting 12 bits per canonical k-mer and streaming 31-mer queries up to 4.9x faster than SSHash. Three further preprints apply compressed-space matching to assemblies and reads: an algorithm for SMEMs and MEMs across terabase pangenome assemblies via BWT run-length indexing, ms2 with move structures for matching statistics and SMEMs, and SIFT, which uses closed-syncmer parsing to select haplotypes for T2T patching. What is new is batch updating of colored indexes without original sequences and smaller, faster k-mer dictionaries.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
